WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.108
Learn to identify common features of graphs that use many-to-one correspondence and

00:00:05.108 --> 00:00:10.016
use that understanding to draw bar graphs or pictographs, complete with title,

00:00:10.016 --> 00:00:15.742
labelled axes, key or legend, to represent data collected (up to 4 categories of

00:00:15.742 --> 00:00:20.241
data) and use understanding of many-to-one correspondence to solve simple problems

00:00:20.241 --> 00:00:24.739
(how many altogether, comparing, or take apart problems) requiring interpretation of

00:00:24.739 --> 00:00:28.829
many-to- one bar graphs (up to 4 categories of data)

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:35.910
A bar chart displays banana equals 36. Which bar height should be used? The answer is

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.791
36. The labelled vertical axis must reach the recorded value.

00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:45.993
A class recorded 4 votes for mangoes. How high should its bar be on an axis marked in

00:00:45.993 --> 00:00:48.681
ones? Pause and solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:53.139
The answer is 4. Bar height equals the recorded total.
